Task: Add diagnostics and example workflows

Summary:
- Added a runnable end-to-end diagnostics workflow example under bindings/typescript/examples/diagnostics-workflow.ts.
- The example discovers a stable model, fits it, predicts, simulates, summarizes, and diagnoses from the fitted state.
- Added a formatted report helper so users can run the example as a simple CLI workflow.
- Documented the example usage in bindings/typescript/README.md.
- Added a test that exercises the end-to-end example and verifies the rendered diagnostics report.

Files:
- bindings/typescript/README.md
- bindings/typescript/examples/diagnostics-workflow.ts
- bindings/typescript/test/diagnostics-workflow.test.ts

Validation:
- npm run typecheck
- npx vitest run --no-cache --coverage

Why:
- The TypeScript bindings now include a concrete user-facing workflow that demonstrates discovery through diagnostics while staying thin and delegating all model semantics to the shared kernel bridge.
